"SS-21/F/why": "Binds the total length of another bar mark to the role shown in the drawing.",
"SS-22": "At the crest at the top of section I—I, take the right-most point of the arc and the tangent point between the arc and the inclined straight segment below it, and find the arc length and the chord length between these two points; also find the opening area of the slot shown in view A2. Compute the arc with the marked radius; lengths in mm and area in mm², to 1 decimal place. Which values does the set of results contain?",
"SS-22/A/why": "44.1 = 2 × 27 × sin 54.69°: it doubles the central angle of 54.69° from the chosen right-most point to the lower tangent point to 109.38° before taking the chord, which widens the stated end points; the chord here is 24.8, and no symmetry of the upper half of the crest needs to be assumed.",
"SS-22/C/why": "16.6 = 27 × (90 − 54.69) × π/180 takes the 35.31° of the inclined segment against the horizontal for the central angle from the right-most point to the lower tangent point; the angle in the drawing is measured from the vertical, and the target is 25.8.",
"SS-22/D/why": "432.0 = 24 × 18 is the area of the bounding rectangle of the A2 slot and includes the four corners outside the rounded ends; the slot consists of a rectangle 18 wide with a straight middle part of 24 − 18 = 6 and two semicircles of radius 9, area 6 × 18 + π × 9² = 362.469005 → 362.5, not listed.",
"SS-22/E/why": "254.5 = π × 9² counts only the full circle formed by the two semicircular ends of the A2 slot and omits the 18 × 6 = 108 rectangle in between; the true value 362.5 is not listed.",
"SS-23": "In the row of single-bar details along the bottom of the sheet, count the separate bar diagrams from left to right; there are seven. Which positions hold a detail that satisfies both conditions: the bar itself has a straight leg in the vertical direction of the sheet, and its diameter in the quantity table of the abutment cap is Φ12? (Leaders, dimension lines and break symbols that shorten a length are not bar legs.)",
