"SS-35": "From the annotations on this sheet alone, without scaling off the schematic, which of the following geometric quantities cannot be uniquely determined?",
"SS-35/A": "Net cross-sectional area of the right side ditch of the cut section, from ditch bottom to ditch top",
"SS-35/B": "Horizontal distance from the outer edge of the right shoulder to the right toe of slope, fill section",
"SS-35/C": "Top width of the right side ditch, cut section",
"SS-35/D": "Horizontal projection of the left slope in the side-ditch detail",
"SS-35/D/why": "Applies to the left slope the limitation of the right slope, whose ratio n1 is not given; the left slope projects 50 × 1 = 50 cm horizontally and is determined.",
"SS-35/E": "Total carriageway width of the fill section",
"SS-35/E/why": "Confuses the undetermined extent of the fill toe with the determined extent of the carriageway. The carriageway is 175 + 175 = 350 cm wide and is determined.",
"SS-35/F": "Horizontal distance from the road centreline to the outer edge of the right shoulder, fill section",
"SS-35/F/why": "Confuses the unknown distance to the toe with the distance to the shoulder edge; the latter is 175 + 50 = 225 cm and is determined.",
"SS-36": "Regarding the local segments of the cap-beam reinforcement of pier No. 5, which of the following statements are correct?",
"SS-36/A": "The sparse zone on the left, in the longitudinal direction, is 100 cm long",
"SS-36/A/why": "Applies the dense spacing of 10 to the 10 intervals of the sparse zone; the true value is 150.",
"SS-36/B": "The left-most dense zone, in the longitudinal direction, is 380 cm long",
"SS-36/C": "The horizontal projection of the inclined segment at the lower left end of the cage is 96.5 cm",
"SS-36/C/why": "Takes the dimension datum of the upper edge; the correct value is 114.9.",
"SS-36/D": "The central dense zone, in the longitudinal direction, is 410 cm long",
"SS-36/E": "The horizontal high segment of the continuous bent-up bar over the middle column is 120 cm long",
"SS-36/E/why": "Takes the adjacent segments of 60 on either side as part of the plateau; the correct value is 80.",
"SS-36/F": "The centre distance between the first and the last bar of the row of longitudinal bars inside the top projection is 88.8 cm",
"SS-36/F/why": "Binds the pitch of 11.1 of the other side; the correct value is 86.4.",
"SS-37": "Regarding the segment layout of the abutment-cap reinforcement, which of the following statements are correct?",
"SS-37/A": "The distance between the centres of the first and the last bar of a transverse row of longitudinal bars is 105 cm",
"SS-37/A/why": "Takes the vertical segment 105; transversely it is 156.",
"SS-37/B": "The marked length of the dense segment in the middle, in the longitudinal direction, is 390 cm",
