"SS-37/C": "The marked length of the sparse segment on the left, in the longitudinal direction, is 120 cm",
"SS-37/C/why": "Applies the dense spacing of 10 to the 12 intervals of the sparse segment; the correct value is 180.",
"SS-37/D": "The marked length of the left-most dense segment, in the longitudinal direction, is 390 cm",
"SS-37/E": "The high horizontal segment of the continuous bent-up bar over the middle pile is 120 cm long",
"SS-37/E/why": "Counts the two adjacent 60 segments of the inclined projections into the high segment; the true value is 40 + 40 = 80.",
"SS-37/F": "In the dimension chain along the upper edge of the cage, the long middle segment between adjacent pile centres is 560 cm",
"SS-37/F/why": "Takes the pile axis spacing for the clear distance between bend points; the correct value is 360.",
"SS-38": "Regarding the transverse positioning, the support at the continuous end and the local groove of the mid-span girders, which of the following statements are correct?",
"SS-38/A": "The bottom slab of the edge girder at midspan is 28 cm thick",
"SS-38/A/why": "Wrong section position bound; it is actually 18.",
"SS-38/B": "The transverse distance between the two outer edges of the bottom slab of the interior girder is 100 cm",
"SS-38/C": "The arc radius of the drip groove is 10 mm",
"SS-38/C/why": "Reads the horizontal positioning dimension 10 as the radius and applies mm; it is actually 15 mm.",
"SS-38/D": "The distance from the bearing centreline of the edge girder to the outer edge of the top slab on the shorter side is 120 cm",
"SS-38/E": "At the continuous end, the end face of the precast girder at the girder bottom is 60 cm from the pier centreline",
"SS-38/E/why": "Applies the position of the bearing centre to the end face at the girder bottom; it is actually 40.",
"SS-38/F": "At the continuous end, the centreline of the temporary bearing is 40 cm from the pier centreline",
"SS-38/F/why": "Takes the dimension of the solid end face for the centre position; it is actually 60.",
"SS-39": "Which of the following combinations of nozzle elevation, anti-flotation dimension or embedded-part layout of the sewage treatment unit agree with the drawing? The nozzle elevation difference is inlet minus outlet; spans are horizontal projections on the sheet.",
"SS-39/A": "Difference between the marked elevations of the inlet and outlet pipes at the two ends of the unit: 0.111 m.",
"SS-39/B": "The four embedded anchor points: placed between the outside of the two rounded ends of the tank, left and right, and the foundation outline.",
"SS-39/B/why": "Outside each of the two rounded ends of the tank there is an end strip of 500, but these four anchor points are not there; they are outside the two long sides, top and bottom, and the 500 zones at the ends must not be confused with the 500 zones along the sides.",
"SS-39/C": "Difference between the marked elevations of the inlet and outlet pipes at the two ends of the unit: 0.261 m.",
"SS-39/C/why": "0.261 = −0.300 − (−0.561), where −0.300 is marked at the recessed shoulder on top of the tank, not at the inlet nozzle at the left end; the inlet pipe is marked −0.450, so the difference is 0.111 m.",
"SS-39/D": "In the anti-flotation detail, the span between the outermost ends of the two horizontal end legs of the folded member below the base slab: 400 mm.",
"SS-39/D/why": "The horizontal chain 400, 300, 400 of the anti-flotation detail spans, in turn, the left horizontal end leg, the distance between the lower ends of the two inclined legs, and the right horizontal end leg; the span between the two outermost ends is 1100 mm. 400 covers only the horizontal end leg of one side and leaves out the other two segments.",
"SS-39/E": "The four embedded anchor points: placed between the outside of the two long sides of the tank and the foundation outline.",
"SS-39/F": "In the anti-flotation detail, the span between the outermost ends of the two horizontal end legs of the folded member below the base slab: 300 mm.",
"SS-39/F/why": "300 spans only between the lower ends of the two inclined legs and does not reach the outermost ends of the left and right horizontal end legs; the whole outer span is 400 + 300 + 400 = 1100 mm.",
